<p data-part="paragraph">The swimming hole is a [x]-minute walk down from the Hearth. It is cold. It is deep enough to swim in through most of the year and shallow enough to stand up in. There is nobody watching it, so you swim at your own risk, and after heavy rain the current gets strong enough that we close it. Ask at the Hearth before you go down.</p>
